#. type: Title ==
#: pages/index.adoc:47
#, no-wrap
msgid "Responsibilities"
msgstr "Ansvar"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:52
#| msgid ""
#| "*Its primary role is to identify the short, medium, and long term goals\n"
#| "of the Fedora community and to organize and enable the project to best\n"
#| "achieve them.* This is done in consultation with the entire Fedora\n"
#| "community through transparent, public discussion.\n"
msgid ""
"The {team_name} is responsible for issues of strategic importance for Fedora"
" that require leadership and coordination across the various teams and sub-"
"projects to achieve.  *Its primary role is to identify the short, medium, "
"and long term goals of the Fedora community and to organize and enable the "
"project to best achieve them*.  This is done in consultation with the entire"
" Fedora community through transparent, public discussion."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} ansvarar för frågor av strategisk betydelse för Fedora som "
"kräver ledarskap och samordning mellan de olika teamen och delprojekten. "
"*Dess främsta roll är att identifiera Fedora-gemenskapens mål på kort, "
"medellång och lång sikt och att organisera och ge projektet förutsättningar "
"att bäst uppnå dem.* Detta sker i samråd med hela Fedora-gemenskapen genom "
"öppna, offentliga diskussioner."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:56
#| msgid ""
#| "The Council also decides on issues regarding use of the Fedora *trademarks*,"
#| " is responsible for final *arbitration of complaints* related to project "
#| "policies and for *settling disputes* escalated from other committees or "
#| "subgroups, and may handle *sensitive legal or personnel issues* which "
#| "require research and discussion to protect the interests of the Fedora "
#| "Project or its sponsor(s)."
msgid ""
"{team_name} members engage with people across the community to make sure "
"Fedora is functioning smoothly and that teams are empowered to do "
"interesting and meaningful things.  They decide on issues regarding use of "
"the Fedora *trademarks*, are responsible for final *arbitration of "
"complaints* related to project policies and for *settling disputes* "
"escalated from other committees or subgroups.  They may handle *sensitive "
"legal or personnel issues* which require research and discussion to protect "
"the interests of the Fedora Project or its sponsors."
msgstr ""
"Medlemmarna i {team_name} samverkar med personer i hela gemenskapen för att "
"säkerställa att Fedora fungerar väl och att teamen får möjlighet att göra "
"intressanta och meningsfulla saker. De fattar beslut i frågor om "
"användningen av Fedoras *varumärken*, ansvarar för slutlig *prövning av "
"klagomål* kopplade till projektets policyer och för att *lösa tvister* som "
"har eskalerats från andra kommittéer eller undergrupper. De kan hantera "
"*känsliga juridiska frågor eller personalfrågor* som kräver efterforskning "
"och diskussion för att skydda Fedora-projektets eller dess sponsorers "
"intressen."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:59
msgid ""
"To support project efforts with more ambitious scope, the {team_name} "
"sponsors xref:project::initiatives.adoc[Community Initiatives] proposed by "
"the community.  {team_name} members serve as "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc#proposing-sponsors[Executive Sponsors] for "
"these Initiatives, working personally to ensure that the "
"<<composition\\--initiative-leads,Leads>> have everything they need to "
"succeed."
msgstr ""
"För att stödja projektinsatser med mer ambitiös omfattning sponsrar "
"{team_name} xref:project::initiatives.adoc[gemenskapsinitiativ] som föreslås"
" av gemenskapen. Medlemmar i {team_name} fungerar som "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc#proposing-sponsors[verkställande sponsorer] "
"för dessa initiativ och arbetar personligen för att se till att "
"<<composition\\--initiative-leads,initiativledarna>> har allt de behöver för"
" att lyckas."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:61
#| msgid ""
#| "The Council *governs Fedora's financial resources*, working with our "
#| "sponsor(s) to establish an annual budget allocated to support Fedora "
#| "initiatives, including Fedora Ambassadors, Fedora-managed events, and other "
#| "activities which advance the project's goals."
msgid ""
"The {team_name} *governs Fedora’s financial resources*, working with our "
"sponsor to establish an annual budget allocated to support these "
"Initiatives, various Fedora teams and programs, Fedora-managed events, and "
"other activities which advance the Fedora Strategy."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} *förvaltar Fedoras ekonomiska resurser* och arbetar med vår "
"sponsor för att fastställa en årlig budget som fördelas för att stödja dessa"
" initiativ, olika Fedora-team och program, evenemang som hanteras av Fedora "
"och andra aktiviteter som främjar Fedora-strategin."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:63
msgid ""
"The {team_name} is also responsible for developing, tracking, and updating "
"the Fedora Strategy."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} ansvarar också för att utveckla, följa upp och uppdatera Fedora-"
"strategin."

#. type: Title ==
#: pages/index.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Making Decisions"
msgstr "Ta beslut"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:71
msgid "Consensus decision-making aims to be:"
msgstr "Konsensusstyrt beslutsfattande syftar till:"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:74
#, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "*Agreement Seeking:* A consensus decision-making process attempts to help "
#| "everyone get what they need.\n"
msgid ""
"*Agreement Seeking:*\n"
"A consensus decision-making process attempts to help everyone get what they need.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Söka samförstånd:*\n"
"En konsensusbaserad beslutsprocess försöker hjälpa alla att få det de behöver.\n"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:76
#, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "*Collaborative:* Participants contribute to a shared proposal and shape it "
#| "into a decision that meets the concerns of all group members as much as "
#| "possible.\n"
msgid ""
"*Collaborative:*\n"
"Participants contribute to a shared proposal and shape it into a decision that meets the concerns of all group members as much as possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Samarbete:*\n"
"Deltagarna bidrar till ett gemensamt förslag och formar det till ett beslut som så långt som möjligt tar hänsyn till alla gruppmedlemmars farhågor.\n"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:78
#, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "*Cooperative:* Participants in an effective consensus process should strive "
#| "to reach the best possible decision for the group and all of its members, "
#| "rather than competing for personal preferences.\n"
msgid ""
"*Cooperative:*\n"
"Participants in an effective consensus process should strive to reach the best possible decision for the group and all of its members, rather than competing for personal preferences.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Samverkan:*\n"
"Deltagare i en effektiv konsensusprocess bör sträva efter att nå det bästa möjliga beslutet för gruppen och alla dess medlemmar i stället för att konkurrera om personliga preferenser.\n"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "*Egalitarian:* All members of a consensus decision-making body should be "
#| "afforded, as much as possible, equal input into the process. All members "
#| "have the opportunity to present, and amend  proposals.\n"
msgid ""
"*Egalitarian:*\n"
"All members of a consensus decision-making body should be afforded, as much as possible, equal input into the process.\n"
"All members have the opportunity to present, and amend  proposals.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Jämlikhet:*\n"
"Alla medlemmar i ett organ som fattar beslut genom konsensus bör så långt som möjligt få lika stort inflytande över processen.\n"
"Alla medlemmar har möjlighet att lägga fram och ändra förslag.\n"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:83
#, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "*Inclusive:* As many stakeholders as possible should be involved in the "
#| "consensus decision-making process.\n"
msgid ""
"*Inclusive:*\n"
"As many stakeholders as possible should be involved in the consensus decision-making process.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Inkluderande:*\n"
"Så många intressenter som möjligt bör delta i den konsensusbaserade beslutsprocessen.\n"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:85
#, no-wrap
#| msgid ""
#| "*Participatory:* The consensus process should actively solicit the input and"
#| " participation of all decision-makers\n"
msgid ""
"*Participatory:*\n"
"The consensus process should actively solicit the input and participation of all decision-makers.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Deltagande:*\n"
"Konsensusprocessen bör aktivt efterfråga synpunkter och deltagande från alla beslutsfattare.\n"

#. type: delimited block *
#: pages/index.adoc:87
msgid ""
"— from https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consensus_decision-"
"making#Objectives[Wikipedia on Consensus decision-making]"
msgstr ""
"— från https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consensus_decision-"
"making#Objectives[Wikipedia on Consensus decision-making]"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:92
#| msgid ""
#| "Many basic decisions are made through a process known as “*lazy approval*”, "
#| "in which general consent is assumed unless valid objections are raised "
#| "within a period of time — generally three to seven days, although the "
#| "timeframe should be stated each time and should be proportionate to the "
#| "impact of the action. This process is used for decisions with short-term "
#| "consequences and which can be easily reversed.  Any project member can ask "
#| "for the deadline to be extended or the decision escalated to require full "
#| "consensus."
msgid ""
"Many basic decisions are made through a process known as “*lazy approval*”, "
"in which general consent is assumed unless valid objections are raised "
"within a period of time — generally three to seven days, although the "
"timeframe should be stated each time and should be proportionate to the "
"impact of the action.  This process is used for decisions with short-term "
"consequences and which can be easily reversed.  Any project member can ask "
"for the deadline to be extended or the decision escalated to require full "
"consensus."
msgstr ""
"Många grundläggande beslut fattas genom en process som kallas ”*tyst "
"godkännande*”, där allmänt samtycke förutsätts om inga giltiga invändningar "
"framförs inom en viss tid – vanligtvis tre till sju dagar. Tidsramen bör "
"alltid anges och stå i proportion till åtgärdens påverkan. Processen används"
" för beslut med kortsiktiga konsekvenser som enkelt kan återställas. Alla "
"projektmedlemmar kan begära att tidsfristen förlängs eller att beslutet "
"lyfts till en process som kräver full konsensus."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:98
#| msgid ""
#| "More significant decisions are made through a process of *full consensus*. "
#| "In order to pass, these decisions need three positive votes (+3) and _no_ "
#| "negative votes (-1). A negative vote immediately halts the process and "
#| "requires discussion. Therefore, in order to remain valid, negative votes "
#| "must be supported with a specific concerns about the proposal, and "
#| "suggestions for what could be changed in order to make the proposal "
#| "acceptable. A vote of “0” is sometimes used to indicate a disagreement but "
#| "willingness to stand aside; this should also be accompanied with an "
#| "explanation."
msgid ""
"More significant decisions are made through a process of *full consensus*.  "
"In order to pass, these decisions need three positive votes (+3) and _no_ "
"negative votes (-1).  A negative vote immediately halts the process and "
"requires discussion.  Therefore, in order to remain valid, negative votes "
"must be supported with a specific concerns about the proposal, and "
"suggestions for what could be changed in order to make the proposal "
"acceptable.  A vote of “0” is sometimes used to indicate a disagreement but "
"willingness to stand aside; this should also be accompanied with an "
"explanation."
msgstr ""
"Viktigare beslut fattas genom *full konsensus*. För att ett sådant beslut "
"ska godkännas krävs tre positiva röster (+3) och _inga_ negativa röster "
"(-1). En negativ röst stoppar omedelbart processen och kräver diskussion. "
"För att förbli giltig måste därför en negativ röst åtföljas av konkreta "
"farhågor om förslaget och förslag på vad som kan ändras för att göra det "
"godtagbart. Rösten ”0” används ibland för att ange oenighet men en vilja att"
" stå åt sidan; även den bör åtföljas av en förklaring."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:101
#| msgid ""
#| "This model matches Fedora's “Friends” foundation, which calls for finding "
#| "acceptable consensus to serve the interests of advancing free software. It "
#| "works because we work together in a community of mutual respect even when we"
#| " disagree."
msgid ""
"This model matches Fedora's “Friends” foundation, which calls for finding "
"acceptable consensus to serve the interests of advancing free software.  It "
"works because we work together in a community of mutual respect even when we"
" disagree."
msgstr ""
"Denna modell motsvarar Fedoras grundprincip ”Friends”, som uppmanar oss att "
"hitta godtagbar konsensus för att främja fri programvara. Den fungerar "
"eftersom vi samarbetar i en gemenskap med ömsesidig respekt, även när vi "
"inte är överens."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:104
#| msgid ""
#| "In general, the Council conducts business in public discussion, and any "
#| "Fedora project member can make negative or positive votes. It is the duty of"
#| " the Council to take concerns raised in this way into serious consideration,"
#| " but only Council members' votes are binding in the final tally."
msgid ""
"In general, the {team_name} conducts business in public discussion, and any "
"Fedora project member can make negative or positive votes.  It is the duty "
"of the {team_name} to take concerns raised in this way into serious "
"consideration, but only {team_name} members' votes are binding in the final "
"tally."
msgstr ""
"I allmänhet bedriver {team_name} sitt arbete i offentliga diskussioner, och "
"alla medlemmar i Fedora-projektet kan lägga negativa eller positiva röster. "
"{team_name} är skyldigt att ta farhågor som framförs på detta sätt på "
"allvar, men endast röster från medlemmarna i {team_name} är bindande i den "
"slutliga räkningen."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:107
#| msgid ""
#| "When consensus can't be reached, the Council may ask the Fedora Project "
#| "Leader to decide on a resolution. Such a request can be made when issues "
#| "leading to negative votes are outstanding and all Council members agree that"
#| " the Council is deadlocked, or if the dispute is unresolved after fourteen "
#| "days and a simple majority of Council members are in favor of the request."
msgid ""
"When consensus cannot be reached, the {team_name} may ask the "
"xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] to decide on a resolution.  Such a "
"request can be made when issues leading to negative votes are outstanding "
"and all {team_name} members agree that the {team_name} is deadlocked, or if "
"the dispute is unresolved after fourteen days and a simple majority of "
"{team_name} members are in favor of the request."
msgstr ""
"När konsensus inte kan nås kan {team_name} be xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project "
"Leader] att avgöra frågan. En sådan begäran kan göras när frågor som leder "
"till negativa röster kvarstår och alla medlemmar i {team_name} är överens om"
" att {team_name} har kört fast, eller om tvisten är olöst efter fjorton "
"dagar och en enkel majoritet av medlemmarna i {team_name} stöder begäran."

#. type: Title ==
#: pages/index.adoc:110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Composition"
msgstr "Sammansättning"

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:113
#, no-wrap
msgid "Community Initiative Leads"
msgstr "Gemenskapsinitiativens ledare"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:118
msgid ""
"On an ongoing basis, including sessions at Flock and in public online "
"meetings, the {team_name} will identify two to four key "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc[Community Initiatives] with a timeframe of "
"approximately eighteen months, and appoint *Community Initiative Leads* for "
"each goal.  Each xref:project::initiatives.adoc[Community Initiative] is "
"represented by one {team_name} seat.  Typically, this seat is filled by the "
"Lead of the Initiative, although it is possible for two people (at most) to "
"share a single {team_name} seat as Co-Leads.  While naturally the people in "
"these roles will focus primarily on their own Initiative, this is a full "
"{team_name} position and Community Initiative Leads are invited to "
"participate in all {team_name} activities and decisions."
msgstr ""
"Löpande, bland annat under sessioner på Flock och i offentliga nätmöten, ska"
" {team_name} identifiera två till fyra centrala "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc[gemenskapsinitiativ] med en tidshorisont på "
"omkring arton månader och utse *gemenskapsinitiativens ledare* för varje "
"mål. Varje xref:project::initiatives.adoc[gemenskapsinitiativ] representeras"
" av en plats i {team_name}. Vanligtvis fylls platsen av initiativets ledare,"
" men två personer kan som mest dela en plats i {team_name} som samordnade "
"ledare. Personerna i dessa roller fokuserar naturligt främst på sitt eget "
"initiativ, men detta är en fullvärdig plats i {team_name}, och ledarna för "
"gemenskapsinitiativen uppmuntras att delta i alla {team_name}s aktiviteter "
"och beslut."

#. type: delimited block =
#: pages/index.adoc:123
msgid ""
"This policy may be surprising, but we have found that this wider engagement "
"connects the specific work to everything going on in Fedora, leading to "
"greater success for the Initiative.  Community Initiative Leads may even "
"serve as Executive Sponsors for other Initiatives."
msgstr ""
"Policyn kan verka överraskande, men vi har funnit att detta bredare "
"engagemang kopplar det specifika arbetet till allt som pågår i Fedora och "
"därmed gör initiativet mer framgångsrikt. Ledare för gemenskapsinitiativ kan"
" till och med fungera som verkställande sponsorer för andra initiativ."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:127
msgid ""
"Community Initiative Leads typically serve on the {team_name} for the "
"duration of their Initiative.  When the Initiative concludes, the "
"{team_name} term also expires."
msgstr ""
"Ledarna för gemenskapsinitiativ sitter vanligen i {team_name} under hela den"
" tid deras initiativ pågår. När initiativet avslutas löper även "
"mandatperioden i {team_name} ut."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:129
msgid ""
"Each Community Initiative Lead is paired with an "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc#proposing-sponsors[Executive Sponsor], who is"
" another member of the {team_name}."
msgstr ""
"Varje ledare för ett gemenskapsinitiativ paras ihop med en "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc#proposing-sponsors[verkställande sponsor], "
"som är en annan medlem av {team_name}."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:133
#| msgid ""
#| "Each objective will be documented with measurable goals, and the objective "
#| "lead is responsible for coordinating efforts to reach those goals, "
#| "evaluating and reporting on progress, and working regularly with all "
#| "relevant groups in Fedora to ensure that progress is made."
msgid ""
"Community Initiatives must be documented with measurable goals.  The "
"Community Initiative Leads are responsible for coordinating efforts to reach"
" those goals, evaluating and reporting on progress, and working regularly "
"with all relevant groups in Fedora to ensure that progress is made.  "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc#proposing-sponsors[Executive Sponsors] are "
"responsible for making sure the Initiative is on track and for removing "
"blockers."
msgstr ""
"Gemenskapsinitiativ måste dokumenteras med mätbara mål. Ledarna för "
"gemenskapsinitiativen ansvarar för att samordna arbetet för att nå målen, "
"utvärdera och rapportera framsteg samt regelbundet samarbeta med alla "
"berörda grupper inom Fedora för att säkerställa framsteg. "
"xref:project::initiatives.adoc#proposing-sponsors[Verkställande sponsorer] "
"ansvarar för att initiativet håller rätt kurs och för att undanröja hinder."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:136
#, no-wrap
msgid "Representatives"
msgstr "Representanter"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:139
#| msgid ""
#| "The Council also includes four representative seats, an *Engineering "
#| "Representative*, a *Mindshare Representative*, and two *Elected "
#| "Representatives*."
msgid ""
"The {team_name} also includes five representative seats: an *Engineering "
"Representative*, a *Mindshare Representative*, a xref:dei:roles:council-"
"advisor.adoc[*DEI Advisor*], and two *Elected Representatives*."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} har också fem representantplatser: en *teknikrepresentant*, en "
"*Mindshare-representant*, en xref:dei:roles:council-advisor.adoc[*DEI-"
"rådgivare*] och två *valda representanter*."

#. type: Title ====
#: pages/index.adoc:141
#, no-wrap
#| msgid "*Diversity & Inclusion Team Representative*\n"
msgid "Engineering & Mindshare Representatives"
msgstr "Teknik- och Mindshare-representanter"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:146
#| msgid ""
#| "“Engineering” and “Mindshare” are broad areas roughly encompassing two of "
#| "the major areas of activity in Fedora. _Engineering_ is the technical work "
#| "related to building and releasing the Fedora operating system and the "
#| "infrastructure related to that. _Mindshare_ includes marketing, design, and "
#| "Fedora Ambassadors — largely activities that happen between Fedora and the "
#| "world at large, with the distribution release cycle serving as a fuel "
#| "source, not the thing that's being worked on."
msgid ""
"“Engineering” and “Mindshare” are broad areas roughly encompassing two of "
"the major areas of activity in Fedora.  _Engineering_ is the technical work "
"related to building and releasing the Fedora operating system and the "
"infrastructure related to that.  _Mindshare_ includes marketing, design, and"
" Fedora Ambassadors — largely activities that happen between Fedora and the "
"world at large, with the distribution release cycle serving as a fuel "
"source, not the thing that's being worked on."
msgstr ""
"”Engineering” och ”Mindshare” är breda områden som ungefär omfattar två av "
"Fedoras viktigaste verksamhetsområden. _Engineering_ är det tekniska arbete "
"som rör att bygga och ge ut Fedora-operativsystemet samt den tillhörande "
"infrastrukturen. _Mindshare_ omfattar marknadsföring, design och Fedora "
"Ambassadors – främst aktiviteter mellan Fedora och omvärlden, där "
"distributionens utgivningscykel fungerar som en källa till energi snarare än"
" som det som arbetet handlar om."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:151
msgid ""
"The engineering and mindshare representatives' responsibility is to "
"represent their areas collectively, _not_ to be just an individual voice "
"that happens to be voted-in by some subset of Fedora.  They are selected by "
"contributors working in those areas, under the rules of the "
"xref:fesco::Fedora_Council_Engineering_Rep.adoc[Fedora Engineering Steering "
"Committee (FESCo)] and the xref:mindshare-"
"committee::procedures/council_rep.adoc[Mindshare Committee], respectively."
msgstr ""
"Teknik- och mindshare-representanternas ansvar är att representera sina "
"respektive områden kollektivt, _inte_ att bara vara en individuell röst som "
"råkar vara invald av någon delmängd av Fedora. De väljs av medarbetare som "
"är aktiva inom dessa områden, i enlighet med reglerna från "
"xref:fesco::Fedora_Council_Engineering_Rep.adoc[Fedoras "
"teknikstyrningskommitté (FESCo)] respektive xref:mindshare-"
"committee::procedures/council_rep.adoc[Mindshare-kommittén]."

#. type: Title ====
#: pages/index.adoc:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "Diversity, Equity, & Inclusion (DEI) Advisor"
msgstr "Rådgivare för mångfald, jämlikhet och inkludering (DEI)"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:158
msgid ""
"The xref:dei:roles:council-advisor.adoc[*Fedora Diversity, Equity, & "
"Inclusion (DEI) Advisor*] is a liaison between the {team_name} and the "
"Fedora community on topics and issues related to diversity, equity, and "
"inclusion in Fedora.  The DEI Advisor works with {team_name} leadership to "
"represent perspectives and voices of the Fedora community in decision-making"
" and project discussions.  This position is appointed by members of the "
"xref:dei::index.adoc[Fedora DEI Team], with the approval of the {team_name}."
msgstr ""
"xref:dei:roles:council-advisor.adoc[*Fedora-rådgivaren för mångfald, "
"jämlikhet och inkludering (DEI)*] är en länk mellan {team_name} och Fedora-"
"gemenskapen i frågor som rör mångfald, jämlikhet och inkludering i Fedora. "
"DEI-rådgivaren arbetar med ledningen för {team_name} för att företräda "
"Fedora-gemenskapens perspektiv och röster i beslutsfattande och "
"projektdiskussioner. Rollen utses av medlemmarna i "
"xref:dei::index.adoc[Fedoras DEI-team] med godkännande av {team_name}."

#. type: Title ====
#: pages/index.adoc:160
#, no-wrap
#| msgid "Representatives"
msgid "Elected Representatives"
msgstr "Valda representanter"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:165
#| msgid ""
#| "The elected positions cover all Fedora subprojects that are not under the "
#| "engineering or mindshare banners, and the community at large. One specific "
#| "responsibility is to represent the voice of individual contributors to the "
#| "Fedora project. Each representative will also work on specific goals which "
#| "she or he brings to the Council as highlighted during the election process."
msgid ""
"The elected positions cover all Fedora subprojects that are not under the "
"engineering or mindshare banners, and the community at large.  One specific "
"responsibility is to represent the voice of individual contributors to the "
"Fedora Project.  Each representative will also work on specific goals which "
"they bring to the {team_name} as highlighted during the election process."
msgstr ""
"De valda platserna omfattar alla Fedora-delprojekt som inte hör till "
"områdena Engineering eller Mindshare samt gemenskapen i stort. Ett särskilt "
"ansvar är att företräda enskilda bidragsgivares röst i Fedora-projektet. "
"Varje representant arbetar också med specifika mål som personen tar med till"
" {team_name} och som lyfts fram under valprocessen."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:170
#| msgid ""
#| "Elections are held twice a year, in concert with the joint Fedora election "
#| "cycle. One seat is selected at each election, and each position has a two-"
#| "election (approximately one year) term. No person who currently holds "
#| "another Council seat can be elected. If a seat becomes vacant, the Council "
#| "will arrange for a temporary replacement."
msgid ""
"Elections are held once per year, in concert with the joint Fedora election "
"cycle.  Two seats are selected at the even-numbered release election, e.g "
"F40, F42, etc, and each position has a two-election (approximately one year)"
" term. This change came into effect from the F40 election, following a "
"council vote on [https://pagure.io/Fedora-Council/tickets/issue/470 this "
"ticket] at the 2024 council hackfest.  No person who currently holds another"
" {team_name} seat can be elected.  If a seat becomes vacant, the {team_name}"
" will arrange for a temporary replacement."
msgstr ""
"Val hålls en gång per år som en del av Fedoras gemensamma valcykel. Två "
"platser väljs vid valet för utgåvor med jämnt nummer, till exempel F40 och "
"F42, och varje plats har en mandatperiod på två val, cirka ett år. Denna "
"ändring började gälla från valet till F40 efter en rådsomröstning om "
"[https://pagure.io/Fedora-Council/tickets/issue/470 detta ärende] vid rådets"
" hackfest 2024. Ingen person som för närvarande innehar en annan plats i "
"{team_name} kan väljas. Om en plats blir vakant ordnar {team_name} en "
"tillfällig ersättare."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:172
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appointed Leadership Positions"
msgstr "Utsedda ledarskapspositioner"

#. type: Title ====
#: pages/index.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
#| msgid "*Fedora Project Leader*\n"
msgid "Fedora Project Leader (FPL)"
msgstr "Fedora Project Leader (FPL)"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:180
#| msgid ""
#| "The xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] serves as the chair of the Council,"
#| " organizing discussion agendas, bringing issues to the table, and "
#| "facilitating the consensus process. He or she is accountable for success in "
#| "all areas of the project, but is not a dictator, benevolent or otherwise. "
#| "The FPL often serves as the public face and collective voice of the project,"
#| " and has a corresponding duty to listen to, understand, and fairly represent"
#| " the collective views and needs of project contributors and stakeholders."
msgid ""
"The xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] (FPL) serves as the chair of the "
"{team_name}, organizing discussion agendas, bringing issues to the table, "
"and facilitating the consensus process.  He or she is accountable for "
"success in all areas of the project, but is not a dictator, benevolent or "
"otherwise.  The FPL often serves as the public face and collective voice of "
"the project, and has a corresponding duty to listen to, understand, and "
"fairly represent the collective views and needs of project contributors and "
"stakeholders."
msgstr ""
"xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] (FPL) är ordförande för {team_name}: "
"hen organiserar diskussionsagendor, lyfter frågor och underlättar "
"konsensusprocessen. FPL ansvarar för framgång inom alla projektets områden, "
"men är ingen diktator, välvillig eller på annat sätt. FPL fungerar ofta som "
"projektets offentliga ansikte och gemensamma röst och har därför en "
"skyldighet att lyssna på, förstå och rättvist företräda de samlade åsikterna"
" och behoven hos projektets bidragsgivare och intressenter."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:182
#| msgid ""
#| "The Fedora Project Leader is hired by Red Hat with the advice and consent of"
#| " the Council."
msgid ""
"The Fedora Project Leader is hired by Red Hat with the advice and consent of"
" the {team_name}."
msgstr ""
"Fedora Project Leader anställs av Red Hat med råd och samtycke från "
"{team_name}."

#. type: Title ====
#: pages/index.adoc:184
#, no-wrap
#| msgid "*Fedora Community Action and Impact Coordinator*\n"
msgid "Fedora Community Architect (FCA)"
msgstr "Fedora Community Architect (FCA)"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:188
#| msgid ""
#| "The xref:fcaic.adoc[Fedora Community Action and Impact Coordinator (FCAIC)] "
#| "initiatives to grow the Fedora user and developer communities, and to make "
#| "Red Hat / Fedora interactions even more transparent and positive. The Fedora"
#| " community budget comes to us through the Red Hat Open Source Program "
#| "Office, and this position facilitates decision-making on how to best focus "
#| "that to meet our collective objectives."
msgid ""
"The xref:fca.adoc[Fedora Community Architect] (FCA) works to grow the Fedora"
" user and developer communities, and to make Red Hat / Fedora interactions "
"even more transparent and positive.  The Fedora community budget comes to us"
" through the Red Hat Open Source Program Office, and this position "
"facilitates decision-making on how to best focus that to meet our collective"
" objectives."
msgstr ""
"xref:fca.adoc[Fedora Community Architect] (FCA) arbetar för att utveckla "
"Fedoras användar- och utvecklargemenskaper och för att göra samspelet mellan"
" Red Hat och Fedora ännu öppnare och mer positivt. Fedora-gemenskapens "
"budget når oss genom Red Hat Open Source Program Office, och rollen "
"underlättar beslutsfattandet om hur medlen bäst kan användas för att nå våra"
" gemensamma mål."

#. type: Title ====
#: pages/index.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
#| msgid "*Fedora Community Action and Impact Coordinator*\n"
msgid "Fedora Operations Architect"
msgstr "Fedora Operations Architect"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:196
#| msgid ""
#| "The "
#| "https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Fedora_Program_Management#Fedora_Program_Manager[FPgM]"
#| " coordinates the planning and scheduling of Fedora releases, and tracks "
#| "changes and features during the development and testing cycle. He or she "
#| "also assists with the creation, maintenance, and execution of formal, "
#| "repeatable Fedora processes. Additionally, the FPgM serves as record keeper "
#| "and secretary for Fedora Council Meetings."
msgid ""
"The xref:foa.adoc[Fedora Operations Architect] (FOA) is employed full-time "
"by Red Hat to assist the community in managing technical changes.  This "
"includes oversight of the Change process, schedule management, "
"communications, and ownership of key strategic efforts.  They also assist "
"with the creation, improvement, maintenance, and execution of formal, "
"repeatable Fedora processes.  Additionally, the Fedora Operations Architect "
"serves as record-keeper and secretary for Fedora Council Meetings."
msgstr ""
"xref:foa.adoc[Fedora Operations Architect] (FOA) är heltidsanställd av Red "
"Hat för att hjälpa gemenskapen att hantera tekniska förändringar. Det "
"omfattar tillsyn över Change-processen, schemaläggning, kommunikation och "
"ansvar för centrala strategiska insatser. FOA hjälper också till att skapa, "
"förbättra, underhålla och genomföra formella, upprepbara Fedora-processer. "
"Dessutom fungerar Fedora Operations Architect som protokollförare och "
"sekreterare vid Fedora Councils möten."

#. type: Title ==
#: pages/index.adoc:199
#, no-wrap
msgid "Coda"
msgstr "Avslutning"

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meetings"
msgstr "Möten"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:207
#| msgid ""
#| "The Fedora Council is not driven by meetings or by tickets, but does hold "
#| "https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Council_Meetings[regular public IRC meetings]"
#| " to discuss current issues, to clear through anything outstanding which can "
#| "be quickly resolved, and to ensure that nothing important is left in limbo. "
#| "All members are be expected to regularly communicate what's going on in "
#| "their area, through blog posts or other public updates."
msgid ""
"The {team_name} is not driven by meetings or by tickets, but does hold "
"link:{url_wiki}/Council_Meetings[regular public meetings] (via a chat system"
" or video call).  The {team_name} discusses current issues, clear through "
"anything outstanding which can be quickly resolved, and to ensure that "
"nothing urgent is left pending.  All members are expected to regularly "
"communicate what is going on in their area, through blog posts or other "
"public updates."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} styrs inte av möten eller ärenden, men håller "
"link:{url_wiki}/Council_Meetings[regelbundna offentliga möten] via ett "
"chattsystem eller videosamtal. {team_name} diskuterar aktuella frågor, reder"
" ut sådant som snabbt kan lösas och säkerställer att inget brådskande lämnas"
" olöst. Alla medlemmar förväntas regelbundet berätta vad som pågår inom "
"deras område genom blogginlägg eller andra offentliga uppdateringar."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:212
msgid ""
"The {team_name} holds a multi-day, face-to-face meeting annually.  All "
"members should strive to attend in person (travel funding is available).  We"
" also often meet for a day before or after other significant Fedora-related "
"conferences (Flock, DevConf.cz).  These meetings are not public, but minutes"
" and summary documents will be provided."
msgstr ""
"{team_name} håller varje år ett fysiskt möte som pågår i flera dagar. Alla "
"medlemmar bör sträva efter att delta personligen; resefinansiering finns. Vi"
" träffas också ofta en dag före eller efter andra betydande Fedora-"
"relaterade konferenser, som Flock och DevConf.cz. Mötena är inte offentliga,"
" men mötesanteckningar och sammanfattande dokument tillhandahålls."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:215
#| msgid ""
#| "Additionally, the Fedora Project Leader will set aside regular times on IRC "
#| "to meet with the community. Attendance is not mandatory for all members but "
#| "is encouraged."
msgid ""
"Additionally, the xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] will set aside "
"regular times to meet with the community.  Attendance is not mandatory for "
"all {team_name} members but is encouraged."
msgstr ""
"Dessutom avsätter xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] regelbunden tid för "
"att träffa gemenskapen. Närvaro är inte obligatorisk för alla medlemmar i "
"{team_name}, men uppmuntras."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:217
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transparency"
msgstr "Öppenhet"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:222
#| msgid ""
#| "The general policy of the Fedora Council is to default to open. Meetings are"
#| " held in public IRC channels, and open to all Fedora users and contributors."
#| " Discussion is held in on a "
#| "https://lists.fedoraproject.org/mailman/listinfo/council-discuss[public "
#| "mailing list] open to all subscribers, and formal decisions will be recorded"
#| " in a public ticket tracking system."
msgid ""
"The general policy of the {team_name} is to default to open.  Most meetings "
"are held in public channels, and open to all Fedora users and contributors."
"  Discussion is held in a link:{team_asynch_communication}[public forum] "
"open to all, and formal decisions will be recorded in a public ticket "
"tracking system."
msgstr ""
"{team_name}s allmänna policy är att som utgångspunkt vara öppet. De flesta "
"möten hålls i offentliga kanaler och är öppna för alla Fedora-användare och "
"bidragsgivare. Diskussioner förs i ett "
"link:{team_asynch_communication}[offentligt forum] som är öppet för alla, "
"och formella beslut dokumenteras i ett offentligt ärendehanteringssystem."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:225
#| msgid ""
#| "Occasionally, when personal, private, or sensitive issues need to be "
#| "discussed, a phone call might be used. A private mailing list and ticket "
#| "tracking instance also exist for these situations, but will also only be "
#| "used when dealing with these uncommon issues."
msgid ""
"Occasionally, when personal, private, or sensitive issues need to be "
"discussed, a video call might be used.  A private mailing list and ticket "
"tracking instance also exist for these situations, but will also only be "
"used when dealing with these uncommon issues."
msgstr ""
"Ibland kan ett videosamtal användas när personliga, privata eller känsliga "
"frågor behöver diskuteras. Det finns också en privat sändlista och en "
"instans för ärendehantering för dessa situationer, men de används endast för"
" dessa ovanliga frågor."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:227
#, no-wrap
msgid "Time Commitment"
msgstr "Tidsåtagande"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:231
#| msgid ""
#| "Serving on the Fedora Council is a significant commitment of time and "
#| "energy. Workload for the various roles will vary, but each will require a "
#| "number of hours every week, and in most cases, the more, the better a "
#| "Council member is able to do the job fully."
msgid ""
"Serving on the {team_name} is a significant commitment of time and energy.  "
"Workload for the various roles will vary, but each will require a number of "
"hours every week, and in most cases, the more, the better a {team_name} "
"member is able to do the job fully."
msgstr ""
"Att ha en plats i {team_name} kräver ett betydande åtagande av tid och "
"energi. Arbetsbördan varierar mellan rollerna, men var och en kräver ett "
"antal timmar varje vecka och i de flesta fall gäller att ju mer tid en "
"medlem i {team_name} kan lägga, desto bättre kan personen fullgöra "
"uppdraget."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:235
#| msgid ""
#| "We recognize that most Fedora community members do not have the luxury of "
#| "working on Fedora full-time or as part of a paid position. The time "
#| "commitment required for these roles comes simply from what is required to "
#| "lead a large project like Fedora, and is not intended to be an artificial "
#| "limit on who can participate. We know that that it can be a _pragmatic_ "
#| "limit, and for that reason, the Council is responsible for extra effort to "
#| "receive, recognize, be responsive to, and meaningfully reward the input of "
#| "contributors offering their individual time."
msgid ""
"We recognize that most Fedora community members do not have the luxury of "
"working on Fedora full-time or as part of a paid position.  The time "
"commitment required for these roles comes simply from what is required to "
"lead a large project like Fedora, and is not intended to be an artificial "
"limit on who can participate.  We know that that it can be a _pragmatic_ "
"limit, and for that reason, the {team_name} is responsible for extra effort "
"to receive, recognize, be responsive to, and meaningfully reward the input "
"of contributors offering their individual time."
msgstr ""
"Vi är medvetna om att de flesta medlemmar i Fedora-gemenskapen inte har "
"möjligheten att arbeta med Fedora på heltid eller som del av en avlönad "
"tjänst. Tidsåtagandet för rollerna följer helt enkelt av vad som krävs för "
"att leda ett stort projekt som Fedora och är inte avsett som en konstgjord "
"begränsning av vem som kan delta. Vi vet att det kan vara en _praktisk_ "
"begränsning och därför ansvarar {team_name} för att göra extra "
"ansträngningar för att ta emot, uppmärksamma, reagera på och på ett "
"meningsfullt sätt belöna bidrag från personer som ger av sin egen tid."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Governance Philosophy"
msgstr "Ledningsfilosofi"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:243
#| msgid ""
#| "To advance free software, we need to provide a sustainable integration of "
#| "free software without cutting corners. By providing a positive first "
#| "impression before and during installation and real use, we support Fedora's "
#| "reputation as a leading and reliable product that attracts future users and "
#| "contributors. To provide that integration and experience we must have a "
#| "clear set of priorities to help all contributors decide how to allocate "
#| "resources and resolve conflicts.  These priorities are not meant to be "
#| "exclusive, or to keep contributors from working on the parts of Fedora that "
#| "matter to them."
msgid ""
"To advance free software, we need to provide a sustainable integration of "
"free software without cutting corners.  By providing a positive first "
"impression before and during installation and real use, we support Fedora's "
"reputation as a leading and reliable product that attracts future users and "
"contributors.  To provide that integration and experience we must have a "
"clear set of priorities to help all contributors decide how to allocate "
"resources and resolve conflicts.  These priorities are not meant to be "
"exclusive, or to keep contributors from working on the parts of Fedora that "
"matter to them."
msgstr ""
"För att främja fri programvara behöver vi erbjuda en hållbar integrering av "
"fri programvara utan genvägar. Genom att ge ett positivt första intryck före"
" och under installationen och vid faktisk användning stärker vi Fedoras "
"anseende som en ledande och tillförlitlig produkt som lockar framtida "
"användare och bidragsgivare. För att erbjuda den integreringen och "
"upplevelsen måste vi ha tydliga prioriteringar som hjälper alla "
"bidragsgivare att fördela resurser och lösa konflikter. Prioriteringarna är "
"inte avsedda att utesluta något eller hindra bidragsgivare från att arbeta "
"med de delar av Fedora som är viktiga för dem."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:247
#| msgid ""
#| "These priorities will sometimes expose gaps where contributors need "
#| "additional assistance, and allow them to seek it both within the community "
#| "and by bringing in additional contributors to help, exclusively on their "
#| "particular interest area if desired. While narrowing our focus in some "
#| "areas, though, we must provide opportunities for exploration to all "
#| "contributors within the framework of our core values and without impeding "
#| "progress."
msgid ""
"These priorities will sometimes expose gaps where contributors need "
"additional assistance, and allow them to seek it both within the community "
"and by bringing in additional contributors to help, exclusively on their "
"particular interest area if desired.  While narrowing our focus in some "
"areas, though, we must provide opportunities for exploration to all "
"contributors within the framework of our core values and without impeding "
"progress."
msgstr ""
"Dessa prioriteringar kommer ibland att synliggöra luckor där bidragsgivare "
"behöver ytterligare hjälp och göra det möjligt för dem att söka den både "
"inom gemenskapen och genom att ta in fler bidragsgivare som kan hjälpa till,"
" om så önskas enbart inom deras särskilda intresseområde. När vi begränsar "
"fokus på vissa områden måste vi dock erbjuda alla bidragsgivare möjligheter "
"att utforska inom ramen för våra kärnvärden och utan att hindra framsteg."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/index.adoc:249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Historical Note"
msgstr "Historisk notering"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/index.adoc:255
#| msgid ""
#| "The previous https://fedoraproject.org/wiki/Board[previous governance "
#| "structure (Fedora Board)] had five members directly appointed by Red Hat and"
#| " five elected at large. The current structure is more complicated but has a "
#| "much greater proportion of members selected by the community by election or "
#| "merit. In the previous board structure, the Fedora Project leader had a "
#| "special veto power; in the current model, all voting members can block on "
#| "issues, with a valid reason. The FPL does not have a special veto, but does "
#| "have a limited power to “unstick” things if consensus genuinely can't be "
#| "reached and a decision needs to be made."
msgid ""
"The previous link:{url_wiki}/Board[previous governance structure (Fedora "
"Board)] had five members directly appointed by Red Hat and five elected at "
"large.  The current structure is more complicated but has a much greater "
"proportion of members selected by the community by election or merit.  In "
"the previous board structure, the xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] had a"
" special veto power; in the current model, all voting members can block on "
"issues, with a valid reason.  The FPL does not have a special veto, but does"
" have a limited power to “unstick” things if consensus genuinely cannot be "
"reached and a decision needs to be made."
msgstr ""
"Den tidigare link:{url_wiki}/Board[styrningsstrukturen (Fedora Board)] hade "
"fem medlemmar som utsågs direkt av Red Hat och fem som valdes av gemenskapen"
" i stort. Den nuvarande strukturen är mer komplicerad men har en betydligt "
"större andel medlemmar som gemenskapen väljer genom val eller meriter. I den"
" tidigare styrelsestrukturen hade xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader] "
"särskild vetorätt. I den nuvarande modellen kan alla röstberättigade "
"medlemmar blockera frågor av giltiga skäl. FPL har inget särskilt veto, men "
"har en begränsad befogenhet att ”lösa upp” situationer när konsensus "
"verkligen inte kan nås och ett beslut behöver fattas."

